<title>UK: UK May natural gas output falls 17 pct - WoodMac.</title>
<headline>UK May natural gas output falls 17 pct - WoodMac.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK natural gas production continued its seasonal decline in May, falling by around 1,500 million cubic feet a day (mmcfd), or over 17 percent from April, to average 7,138 mmcfd, consultants Wood Mackenzie said in its July North Sea Report.</p>
<p>The average demand on the Transco system fell to 6,169 mmcfd in May from 7,541 mmcfd in April. And output from the Morecambe field, owned by Centrica, decreased to 336 mmcfd in May, a drop of 50 percent from April.</p>
<p>Significant output falls were seen at Leman (down 181 mmcfd), Amethyst (down 132 mmcfd), Valiant (down 117 mmcfd), and Victor (down 158 mmcfd).</p>
<p>Gas flowed at the rate of 24 mmcfd from Windermere following first production at the end of April. And first gas also flowed through the new Seal Sands processing plant on Teesside.</p>
